P('angular-kinematics','The turning rate rises steadily','The wheel starts at 1 rad/s and gains 0.5 rad/s each second. After 4 s it reaches 3 rad/s.','Time (s)',[0,4],'Angular velocity (rad/s)',[0,4],[S('Turning rate',[[0,1],[4,3]])]);
B('rolling-energy','Two parts of rolling energy','Moving forward contributes 1 J and turning contributes 0.5 J. Together they make 1.5 J.','Energy (J)',[['Forward motion',1],['Turning',.5],['Total',1.5]]);
P('inverse-square-gravity','Gravity weakens with distance','At 2 million metres the inward acceleration has size 2 m/s². Doubling that distance reduces its size to one quarter.','Centre distance (million m)',[1,4],'Acceleration size (m/s²)',[0,8],[S('Gravity outside the source',sample(r=>8/r**2,1,4))]);
B('orbital-energy','Adding positive and negative energy','With zero potential energy at infinity, 6 MJ plus −12 MJ gives total energy −6 MJ.','Energy (MJ)',[['Kinetic',6],['Potential',-12],['Total',-6]]);
P('fluid-pressure-depth','Deeper water adds pressure','In this water model, each metre adds 10,000 Pa. The line shows pressure added by depth, before adding surface pressure.','Depth (m)',[0,2],'Added pressure (kPa)',[0,20],[S('Water pressure increase',[[0,0],[2,20]])]);
