P('spacetime-diagram','Time goes upward on this graph','The straight history reaches position 600 m when light-speed × time reaches 1000 m. The dashed light history reaches 1000 m in that same time. This graph shows events, not an object’s shape.','Position (m)',[0,1000],'Light-speed × time (m)',[0,1000],[S('Object history',[[0,0],[600,1000]]),S('Light history',[[0,0],[1000,1000]])]);
P('separation-types','Light can cover this separation in time','The event is at position 3 m when light could have covered 5 m. It lies inside the right-moving light limit, so slower-than-light travel can connect these events.','Position (m)',[0,5],'Light-speed × time (m)',[0,5],[S('History connecting the events',[[0,0],[3,5]]),S('Light limit',[[0,0],[5,5]])]);
P('twin-comparison','Add the time on both legs','For this ideal trip, each 5 s laboratory leg adds 4 s to the traveller’s clock. The brief turnaround is ignored. Both lines start at departure.','Laboratory time (s)',[0,10],'Clock reading (s)',[0,10],[S('Travelling clock',[[0,0],[5,4],[10,8]]),S('Laboratory clock',[[0,0],[10,10]])]);
