P('random-decays-smooth-average','Half remain on average','The smooth curve starts at 800 and reaches 400 after one half-life. Real counts vary around this expectation.','Time (half-lives)',[0,3],'Expected remaining nuclei',[0,800],[S('Decay expectation',sample(t=>800*2**(-t),0,3))]);
P('attenuation-removes-unscattered-photons','Half the beam remains at this thickness','The horizontal value combines attenuation coefficient and thickness. At ln(2), about 0.693, the uncollided fraction is 0.5.','Coefficient × thickness (no units)',[0,2],'Uncollided beam fraction',[0,1],[S('Remaining beam',sample(x=>Math.exp(-x),0,2))]);
P('infer-an-original-spectral-ladder','Three levels explain three gaps','The gaps are 2 eV, 3 eV and 5 eV. This possible ladder fits those gaps; it is not a unique full model of the atom. Horizontal spacing is only for drawing.','Label spacing (no physical units)',[0,1],'Energy (eV)',[0,6],[S('Level 0 eV',[[.2,0],[.8,0]]),S('Level 2 eV',[[.2,2],[.8,2]]),S('Level 5 eV',[[.2,5],[.8,5]])]);
P('fit-a-decay-record-cautiously','Two readings support a decay estimate','The dots are the two stated corrected rates. The curve assumes a single exponential with half-life 10 s; measurement uncertainty still matters.','Time since first reading (s)',[0,20],'Corrected rate (1/s)',[0,80],[S('Fitted model',sample(t=>80*2**(-t/10),0,20)),S('Stated readings',[[0,80],[10,40]],{join:false})]);
